1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429768 1077 "selection" 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429768 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429756 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429768 1079 #uuid "9ccdc12a-fbdf-5044-b512-ae9ee21b3e92" 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429769 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429768 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429769 1069 "q-74977" 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429769 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429769 1071 "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ by inspection." 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429769 1072 #uuid "293eb96a-a168-5847-97d0-8739c8726172" 13194139534621 17592186045417 true] [17592186429769 1074 "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{1}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1\\cdot {a}_{2}+1\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{1}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by just $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}},{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\\}.\n$$" 13194139534621 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0ad3f32a-699b-5f19-8537-5ee75cb30b47" 17592186429751 "answer-29b21dda-de01-5604-87d6-f